      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the cast-iron skillet over high heat for 3 minutes until very hot. Add 2 tablespoons of oil. Season the beef strips with cumin and coriander."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the beef in a single layer. Do not stir for 2 minutes. Let it colour well before turning. Cook for another minute. Remove to a plate."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the remaining oil to the pan. Add the onion and stir-fry for 3 minutes over high heat. Add the garlic and ginger and cook for 1 minute more."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the peppers and chilli flakes. Stir-fry for 2 minutes. Add the tomato quarters and cook until just softened, about 1 minute."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Return the beef to the pan. Toss everything together over high heat for 1 minute. Scatter over the rosemary leaves and serve immediately with injera."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Beef is chewy rather than tender"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slice against the grain and do not overcook. Sirloin needs only 3 minutes total over high heat. Longer cooking toughens it."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Pan is smoking excessively"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This is normal for cast iron at high heat. Ensure your kitchen is ventilated. If the smoke alarm is a risk, lower the heat slightly and cook a minute longer per side."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Vegetables are soft and watery"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook in a dry, hot pan and keep everything moving. Adding vegetables while the pan is too cool releases their moisture and they stew instead of fry."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tibs is one of the most popular dishes in Ethiopian restaurants. It comes in many versions from dry and crispy to saucy and soft. The word simply means fried or sauteed. In Addis Ababa, it is often served in the clay pan it was cooked in. Rosemary is widely grown in Ethiopia and used far more in cooking there than elsewhere in Africa."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
